{"matches":[{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-535w-7cp7-47q4","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-535w-7cp7-47q4","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-535w-7cp7-47q4","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82333","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/pull/1438","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/commit/73c1759fa93b87366bc6dbd7abe1b80ddff7d27c","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/releases/tag/v2.3.0"],"description":"multer vulnerable to Denial of Service via oversized array index in field names","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-82333","epss":0.00488,"percentile":0.4001,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-82333","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.3.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.3.0","date":"2026-09-09","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.366},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-82333","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82333","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-535w-7cp7-47q4"],"description":"multer is a middleware for handling multipart/form-data in Node.js. A small multipart request with two specially crafted text field names can make multer's field parser synchronously iterate a maximum-length sparse array, blocking the event loop so the process cannot handle other requests. A large numeric array index in the first field allocates a maximum-length sparse array, and a second field with a non-numeric key then triggers a full-length iteration inside the append-field dependency. All versions before 2.3.0 are affected, and this is a remotely triggerable denial of service. multer 2.3.0 adds an opt-in fieldArrayIndexLimit option that rejects oversized array indexes. Upgrade to multer 2.3.0 and set limits.fieldArrayIndexLimit to the largest array index your application needs to remediate.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-82333","epss":0.00488,"percentile":0.4001,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-82333","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"multer","version":"2.2.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-535w-7cp7-47q4","versionConstraint":"<2.3.0 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.3.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0?package-id=da7379e3f5a4dc5c","name":"multer","version":"2.2.0","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:multer:multer:2.2.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77078","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/commit/87a584e8c8d4da873292635fa1d8c4d78d985b76","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/releases/tag/v2.3.0"],"description":"multer vulnerable to Denial of Service via crafted multipart field names","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77078","epss":0.00488,"percentile":0.40005,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77078","cwe":"CWE-248","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.3.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.3.0","date":"2026-09-09","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.366},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-77078","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77078","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm"],"description":"multer is a middleware for handling multipart/form-data in Node.js. A small multipart request containing two specially crafted text field names can cause an uncaught RangeError (Invalid array length) that terminates the Node.js process. The first field uses a very large numeric array index to allocate a maximum-length sparse array, and a second field then pushes past that length, which throws inside the append-field dependency and is not caught by multer. All versions before 2.3.0 are affected, and the issue is a remotely triggerable denial of service. The issue is fixed in multer 2.3.0. Upgrade to multer 2.3.0 to remediate.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77078","epss":0.00488,"percentile":0.40005,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77078","cwe":"CWE-248","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"multer","version":"2.2.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm","versionConstraint":"<2.3.0 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.3.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0?package-id=da7379e3f5a4dc5c","name":"multer","version":"2.2.0","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:multer:multer:2.2.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Critical","urls":["https://github.com/jshttp/proxy-addr/security/advisories/GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-90711","https://github.com/jshttp/proxy-addr/commit/780911d84d18e2c5fa008ed0c0d387631ec11965","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/jshttp/proxy-addr/releases/tag/v2.0.8"],"description":"proxy-addr vulnerable to IP spoofing via IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnet","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":9.1,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":5.2},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","epss":0.00332,"percentile":0.24328,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","cwe":"CWE-290","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","cwe":"CWE-348","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","cwe":"CWE-697","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.0.8"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.0.8","date":"2026-10-06","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.30046},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-90711","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-90711","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Critical","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/jshttp/proxy-addr/security/advisories/GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h"],"description":"proxy-addr is a Node.js module that determines a request's client address behind trusted reverse proxies, and it backs Express req.ip and req.ips. In versions 1.1.0 through 2.0.7, a trust subnet written in IPv4-mapped IPv6 notation with an IPv4-sized prefix, such as ::ffff:10.0.0.0/8 instead of the correct ::ffff:10.0.0.0/104, is accepted without error but trusts every IPv4 address on the internet rather than the block it names. Because the socket peer then becomes trusted at hop 0, any unauthenticated client can supply an arbitrary X-Forwarded-For header and control the address the application reads, which defeats IP-based access control, rate limiting, geolocation, and audit logging. This is a fail-open regression introduced in version 1.1.0. The issue is fixed in proxy-addr 2.0.8, and users should upgrade to 2.0.8 or later. As a workaround, ensure any IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnet uses a prefix length of at least 97, or express the range in plain IPv4 notation.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":9.1,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":5.2},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","epss":0.00332,"percentile":0.24328,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","cwe":"CWE-290","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","cwe":"CWE-348","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-90711","cwe":"CWE-697","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"proxy-addr","version":"2.0.7"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h","versionConstraint":">=1.1.0,<2.0.8 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.0.8"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/proxy-addr@2.0.7?package-id=ce10aea6db36304a","name":"proxy-addr","version":"2.0.7","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:proxy-addr:proxy-addr:2.0.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:proxy-addr:proxy_addr:2.0.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:proxy_addr:proxy-addr:2.0.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:proxy_addr:proxy_addr:2.0.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:proxy:proxy-addr:2.0.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:proxy:proxy_addr:2.0.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/proxy-addr@2.0.7","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-3pph-fpjx-jg34","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3pph-fpjx-jg34","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-3pph-fpjx-jg34","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-88932","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/commit/53337f9713619ef3381ee6b4e541f926dbaac305","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/releases/tag/v2.4.0"],"description":"multer vulnerable to Denial of Service via orphaned disk writes on aborted uploads","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-88932","epss":0.00532,"percentile":0.43132,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-88932","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-88932","cwe":"CWE-459","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.4.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.4.0","date":"2026-09-29","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.27398},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-88932","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-88932","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-3pph-fpjx-jg34"],"description":"multer is a Node.js middleware for handling multipart/form-data uploads. In versions 2.2.0 through 2.3.0, when a request using disk storage is aborted mid-upload, file writes that complete after multer has already run its abort cleanup are not removed, so each aborted upload can leave an orphaned file on disk. A remote unauthenticated attacker can repeatedly start and abort uploads to accumulate orphaned files and exhaust disk space, causing a denial of service. The issue is fixed in multer 2.4.0, and users should upgrade to 2.4.0 or later.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-88932","epss":0.00532,"percentile":0.43132,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-88932","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-88932","cwe":"CWE-459","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"multer","version":"2.2.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-3pph-fpjx-jg34","versionConstraint":">=2.2.0,<2.4.0 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.4.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0?package-id=da7379e3f5a4dc5c","name":"multer","version":"2.2.0","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:multer:multer:2.2.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77037","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/commit/eef74440b491ef0f976f3d25895e8089ae495df0","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/releases/tag/v2.3.0"],"description":"multer vulnerable to Denial of Service via file descriptor leak on aborted uploads","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77037","epss":0.00347,"percentile":0.26183,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77037","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-77037","cwe":"CWE-459","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.3.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.3.0","date":"2026-09-09","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.26025},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-77037","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77037","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf"],"description":"multer is a middleware for handling multipart/form-data in Node.js. In version 2.2.0, when a disk-backed upload is aborted or truncated before the write stream finishes, multer's disk storage engine removes the visible file but does not close the underlying write file descriptor, leaving a deleted but still open descriptor. A remote attacker able to reach an upload route using the built-in disk storage can send repeated aborted or malformed multipart uploads, each one leaking a file descriptor and retaining disk blocks until the process exits, which can exhaust resources and cause a denial of service. The issue is fixed in multer 2.3.0, which closes the destination write stream on abnormal source termination and defers cleanup until the stream has closed. Upgrade to multer 2.3.0 to remediate.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77037","epss":0.00347,"percentile":0.26183,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77037","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-77037","cwe":"CWE-459","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"multer","version":"2.2.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf","versionConstraint":"=2.2.0 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.3.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0?package-id=da7379e3f5a4dc5c","name":"multer","version":"2.2.0","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:multer:multer:2.2.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/multer@2.2.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-qvfw-j98x-7q72","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qvfw-j98x-7q72","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Low","urls":["https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-qvfw-j98x-7q72","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77063","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/commit/ab6aeae650328cf31799dcfa4c3e116ba8faaacc","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/releases/tag/v2.3.0"],"description":"multer vulnerable to file size limit bypass via async fileFilter race condition","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.7,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77063","epss":0.00233,"percentile":0.1305,"date":"2026-10-07"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-77063","cwe":"CWE-362","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.3.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.3.0","date":"2026-09-09","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.078055},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-77063","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77063","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Low","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-qvfw-j98x-7q72"],"description":"multer is a middleware for handling multipart/form-data in Node.js. When an application uses an asynchronous fileFilter together with the fileSize limit, a race condition in multer's file stream handling can allow a file that exceeds the configured size limit to bypass the size-limit rejection. All versions before 2.3.0 are affected. The impact is limited because the underlying multipart parser still truncates the stream at the size limit, so this is a bypass of the limit rejection rather than uncontrolled resource consumption. The issue is fixed in multer 2.3.0. Upgrade to multer 2.3.0 to remediate.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N